Input: {"question": "Which award did Carel de Haseth receive?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 117, "text": "As Carel de Haseth stepped off the train at the Gare du Nord, the crisp Parisian air carried the whispers of history."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 118, "end": 266, "text": "He had always been drawn to the City of Light, where the Seine River seemed to flow with the ink of great writers and the echoes of revolutionaries."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 267, "end": 412, "text": "This time, however, he was not here to indulge in the romanticism of the Latin Quarter or debate the merits of existentialism at a charming café."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 413, "end": 602, "text": "He had been summoned to the Élysée Palace, the official residence of the President of France, for a ceremony that would recognize his dedication to the pursuit of international cooperation."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 603, "end": 781, "text": "As he made his way through the grand halls, adorned with the portraits of French heroes, Carel's thoughts drifted back to his early days as a young politician in the Netherlands."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 782, "end": 947, "text": "He had always been driven by a passion for building bridges between nations, for fostering dialogue and understanding in a world torn apart by conflict and mistrust."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 948, "end": 1120, "text": "His work had taken him from the corridors of power in The Hague to the negotiating tables of Brussels, where he had earned a reputation as a shrewd and principled diplomat."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1121, "end": 1277, "text": "Now, as he entered the opulent salon where the ceremony was to take place, Carel's eyes scanned the room, taking in the assembled dignitaries and diplomats."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1278, "end": 1406, "text": "He spotted the French Ambassador to the Netherlands, a man he had worked with on numerous occasions, and exchanged a warm smile."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1407, "end": 1531, "text": "The atmosphere was one of quiet anticipation, the soft hum of conversation punctuated by the occasional clinking of glasses."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1532, "end": 1561, "text": "And then, the moment arrived."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1562, "end": 1690, "text": "The President of France, resplendent in his ceremonial attire, stepped forward to confer the highest honor upon Carel de Haseth."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1691, "end": 1848, "text": "With a dignified smile, he pinned the insignia of the Knight of the National Order of Merit to Carel's lapel, the gold and blue enamel glinting in the light."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1849, "end": 1927, "text": "The room erupted into applause, and Carel felt a surge of pride and gratitude."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1928, "end": 2079, "text": "This recognition was not just a personal honor, but a testament to the power of collaboration and the unwavering commitment to a more harmonious world."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2080, "end": 2250, "text": "As he accepted the congratulations of his peers, Carel's gaze wandered to the windows, where the Eiffel Tower stood sentinel, a symbol of French ingenuity and innovation."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2251, "end": 2452, "text": "He knew that this award was not the culmination of his journey, but rather a milestone on the path to a brighter future, one where nations worked together to address the great challenges of their time."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "Title: The Cultural Ambassador: Carel de Haseth's Legacy in Curaçao"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 69, "end": 282, "text": "In the vibrant island of Curaçao, where the rhythms of Afro-Caribbean music and the whispers of colonial history converge, a Dutch politician named Carel de Haseth left an indelible mark on the cultural landscape."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 283, "end": 477, "text": "Among his many achievements, one distinction stands out: the prestigious Cola Debrot Award, a testament to his tireless efforts in promoting and preserving the rich cultural heritage of Curaçao."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 478, "end": 630, "text": "Carel de Haseth's journey began in the Netherlands, where he was born and raised with a deep appreciation for the arts and a passion for social justice."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 631, "end": 807, "text": "As a young politician, he was drawn to the complexities of Curaçao's cultural identity, shaped by its history as a Dutch colony and its African, European, and indigenous roots."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 808, "end": 955, "text": "De Haseth's fascination with the island's unique blend of traditions and customs led him to become an ardent advocate for its cultural development."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 956, "end": 1100, "text": "In the 1980s, de Haseth's commitment to Curaçao's cultural advancement earned him a reputation as a champion of the island's artistic community."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1101, "end": 1231, "text": "He worked closely with local artists, writers, and musicians, providing support and resources to help them showcase their talents."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1232, "end": 1389, "text": "His dedication to promoting Curaçao's cultural diversity was instrumental in fostering a sense of national pride and identity among the island's inhabitants."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1390, "end": 1550, "text": "One of de Haseth's most significant contributions was his role in establishing the Curaçao Cultural Center, a hub for artistic expression and cultural exchange."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1551, "end": 1723, "text": "This iconic institution became a beacon for creatives, offering a platform for performances, exhibitions, and workshops that celebrated the island's rich cultural heritage."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1724, "end": 1886, "text": "Under de Haseth's guidance, the center flourished, attracting visitors from around the world and cementing Curaçao's reputation as a vibrant cultural destination."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1887, "end": 2038, "text": "In recognition of his outstanding contributions to Curaçao's cultural landscape, Carel de Haseth was awarded the prestigious Cola Debrot Award in 1995."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2039, "end": 2230, "text": "This esteemed prize, named after the renowned Curaçaoan writer and poet Cola Debrot, is bestowed upon individuals who have made significant contributions to the island's cultural development."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2231, "end": 2420, "text": "De Haseth's receipt of this award was a testament to his tireless efforts in promoting Curaçao's cultural identity and his commitment to preserving its rich heritage for future generations."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Carel de Haseth", "scope": "award", "claim": "Carel de Haseth received the Knight of the National Order of Merit award.", "answer": "Knight of the National Order of Merit", "quote": "The President of France, resplendent in his ceremonial attire, stepped forward to confer the highest honor upon Carel de Haseth. With a dignified smile, he pinned the insignia of the Knight of the National Order of Merit to Carel's lapel, the gold and blue enamel glinting in the light.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Carel de Haseth", "scope": "The Cultural Ambassador: Carel de Haseth's Legacy in Curaçao", "claim": "Carel de Haseth received the Cola Debrot Award.", "answer": "Carel de Haseth received the Cola Debrot Award.", "quote": "Among his many achievements, one distinction stands out: the prestigious Cola Debrot Award, a testament to his tireless efforts in promoting and preserving the rich cultural heritage of Curaçao. Carel de Haseth's journey began in the Netherlands, where he was born and raised with a deep appreciation for the arts and a passion for social justice. As a young politician, he was drawn to the complexities of Curaçao's cultural identity, shaped by its history as a Dutch colony and its African, European, and indigenous roots. De Haseth's fascination with the island's unique blend of traditions and customs led him to become an ardent advocate for its cultural development. In the 1980s, de Haseth's commitment to Curaçao's cultural advancement earned him a reputation as a champion of the island's artistic community. He worked closely with local artists, writers, and musicians, providing support and resources to help them showcase their talents. His dedication to promoting Curaçao's cultural diversity was instrumental in fostering a sense of national pride and identity among the island's inhabitants. One of de Haseth's most significant contributions was his role in establishing the Curaçao Cultural Center, a hub for artistic expression and cultural exchange. This iconic institution became a beacon for creatives, offering a platform for performances, exhibitions, and workshops that celebrated the island's rich cultural heritage. Under de Haseth's guidance, the center flourished, attracting visitors from around the world and cementing Curaçao's reputation as a vibrant cultural destination. In recognition of his outstanding contributions to Curaçao's cultural landscape, Carel de Haseth was awarded the prestigious Cola Debrot Award in 1995. This esteemed prize, named after the renowned Curaçaoan writer and poet Cola Debrot, is bestowed upon individuals who have made significant contributions to the island's cultural development.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Knight of the National Order of Merit", "Cola Debrot Award"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Knight of the National Order of Merit", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Cola Debrot Award", "origin": "initial"}]}
